      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "District 3, the East End, is clearly the most vulnerable hotspot due to its high density and concentration of low-income, multi-generational housing, which facilitates rapid spread. The main drivers there will be close-quarters living and essential worker exposure. District 2 is also a significant risk due to its mix of service industry jobs, which means high daily contact. You should focus initial efforts on District 3 to contain the most concentrated outbreak, while also targeting District 2 to manage the working-class spread.",
      "source": "target",
