      "content": "That makes sense from a density perspective. I'm looking deeper into the \"cultural\" side of the variables for the simulation, though. In District 3 specifically, given the high concentration of Hispanic and Black residents, do you think there are specific lifestyle or community behaviors—like certain types of social gatherings, religious practices, or even general hygiene/living standards—that we should factor in as higher-risk variables for the transmission rate? I want the model to be as realistic as possible about how the community functions.",
